<title>GERMANY: Krupp details results by division.</title>
<headline>Krupp details results by division.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			  208	vs 505</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			 108	vs 360</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities   336	vs 644</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (DVFA/SG)	  18 DM    vs 26 DM</p>
<p>    Dividend (proposed)		     5	  vs 5</p>
<p>Breakdown of pre-tax profit by division:</p>
<p>    Mechanical engineering		  159	vs 113</p>
<p>    Fabricating				 111	vs 116</p>
<p>    Plant construction			88	 vs 61</p>
<p>    Automotive				  105	vs 120</p>
<p>Steel:</p>
<p>	Stainless flat/Nirosta		152	vs 466</p>
<p>	Quality steel, profiles	     208 loss vs 94</p>
<p>    Trading				     17	 vs 68</p>
<p>    Parent, other units combined loss   88 loss  vs 394 loss</p>
<p>  Group sales				   24,038   vs 23,535</p>
<p>Breakdown of sales by division:</p>
<p>    Mechanical engineering		  2,800    vs 2,900</p>
<p>    Fabricating				 3,000    vs 3,000</p>
<p>    Plant construction			2,500    vs 1,800</p>
<p>    Automotive				  3,000    vs 2,900</p>
<p>Steel:</p>
<p>	Stainless flat/Nirosta		5,100    vs 3,800</p>
<p>	Quality steel, profiles	     5,200    vs 5,900</p>
<p>    Trading				     5,600    vs 6,600</p>
<p>    Parent, other units combined	  900	vs 900</p>
<p>    Financial debt			    2,900    vs 3,600</p>
<p>    Group workforce on Dec 31	     69,608   vs 66,352</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German steel and engineering group is Fried. Krupp AG Hoesch-Krupp. The total sales and profit data were reported earlier.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 2609750 (c) Reuters Limited 1996</p>
